   902	    # them first was a design bug: on 2026-10-20 a slow `op read` under launchd held the
   903	    # startup path for minutes, so the port never opened and the service looked dead
   904	    # while the process was perfectly healthy. Binding first means /stats answers at
   905	    # once, a span that cannot be forwarded is counted rather than lost, and the thing
   906	    # is diagnosable from outside. KeyCache's backoff keeps the retries cheap.
   907	    if upstreams and not args.dry_run:
